  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Root cause located in `lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`: the `install()` function builds `collection_tar._ansible_normalized_cache = {m.name.removesuffix(os.path.sep): m for m in collection_tar.getmembers()}` (annotated as a deprecated CPython-tarfile-bug workaround, `core_version='2.18' python_version='3.11'`), and `_extract_tar_dir()` looks up directories via `tar._ansible_normalized_cache[dirname]` instead of the standard `tar.getmember()`. The existing test file `test/units/cli/galaxy/test_collection_extract_tar.py` mocks this exact `_ansible_normalized_cache` attribute, confirming the fragile custom-cache dependency described in the bug report.",
